  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37131460",
      "title": "Introducing Maps & \"for\" Loops",
      "lectureOrder": 81,
      "videoOrder": 75,
      "sourceHash": "fd28cd1588bb72446fedbe1e29baec746a8f7b1f8326f0b433d3fb9e4c3f8970",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "Now in order to output some useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 7.38,
          "en": "information in this results screen here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.38,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "we now have to kind of combine the chosen answers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "with the questions that we have in this separate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 17.43,
          "en": "questions.dart file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "And for that, I'll add a new method here to results screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 25.71,
          "en": "and I'll introduce you to a new data type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.71,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "But let's start with the method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 32.467,
          "en": "I'll add a method called get summary data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 36.993,
          "en": "The name of course as always, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.07,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "And in this method here, I wanna return a list of values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 47.49,
          "en": "but now not a list of strings or a list of widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 51.39,
          "en": "but instead a list of so-called maps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 51.39,
          "end": 55.14,
          "en": "And that's now not a map as in Google Maps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 55.14,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "but instead in programming, a map is a very simple data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "structure that maps values to keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 67.97,
          "en": "And in dart, map, just like list, is actually a generic type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.06,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "where you specify the type of your keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 75.3,
          "en": "and the type of your values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 75.3,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "So we need another pair of opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "and closing angle brackets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 81.53999999999999,
          "en": "Therefore, we have some nested angle brackets here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 84.96000000000001,
          "en": "which is absolutely something you can have in dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.96000000000001,
          "end": 89.16,
          "en": "And this inner pair of angle brackets now belongs to map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.16,
          "end": 92.64,
          "en": "And for my keys, I'll have a bunch of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.64,
          "end": 96.75,
          "en": "So the keys in my map will simply be string identifiers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.75,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "but for the values, I'll have different types of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "I will have strings and also numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "for these different keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "And therefore here, the second type I specify for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 112.92,
          "en": "map generic type after this comma here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.92,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "which is the type of values that will be stored in this map",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 120.42,
          "en": "should be object written like this with a capital O.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.42,
          "end": 124.08,
          "en": "Since all values in dart are objects at the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.08,
          "end": 126.39,
          "en": "this is a pretty flexible type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126.39,
          "end": 130.23,
          "en": "that actually allows all kinds of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "And this allows me to store different kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 134.97,
          "en": "of values in this map here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "So that this map can simply be used as a data structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 143.24,
          "en": "that groups different kinds of key value pairs together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 146.91,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could create a brand new class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 150.39,
          "en": "that defines how our summary objects should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.39,
          "end": 152.34,
          "en": "And then we could instantiate a bunch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.34,
          "end": 153.87,
          "en": "of summary objects here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.87,
          "end": 157.2,
          "en": "and that would definitely also be a great approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 161.13,
          "en": "But I also want to introduce you to this map value and type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 163.383,
          "en": "and that's why I'm using this approach here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.55,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "So get summary data should return such a list of maps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 171.42000000000002,
          "en": "Now to generate this list here, I'll start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.42000000000002,
          "end": 174.12,
          "en": "with an empty list, which I'll store in a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 174.12,
          "end": 177.69299999999998,
          "en": "or in a final variable to be precise, called summary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.65,
          "end": 183.65,
          "en": "And the type of this list here should be this type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.78,
          "end": 187.203,
          "en": "since in the end I plan on returning summary here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "But of course in between creating it as an empty list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "and returning it, I also wanna populate that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "And for that, we'll use a new dart feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "which we haven't seen before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 201.633,
          "en": "We'll create a for loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 206.43,
          "en": "Now, early in this section we saw if statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.43,
          "end": 208.77,
          "en": "to run some code conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.77,
          "end": 211.77,
          "en": "And if statements are so-called control structures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.77,
          "end": 215.19299999999998,
          "en": "because they allow you to control the code execution flow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "Another kind of control structure supported by dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 224.19,
          "en": "and many other programming languages as well, are for loops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 227.37,
          "en": "With the four keywords, you create such a loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 229.89,
          "en": "and a for loop simply allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 229.89,
          "end": 233.553,
          "en": "to execute a certain code snippet multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 237,
          "en": "To do that, you also add parenthesis here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 237,
          "end": 239.61,
          "en": "And between these parentheses you add your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 239.61,
          "end": 242.85,
          "en": "for loop configuration, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.85,
          "end": 246.27,
          "en": "This configuration consists of three parts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.27,
          "end": 249.3,
          "en": "The first part is a helper variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 249.3,
          "end": 251.55,
          "en": "that's created for this loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.55,
          "end": 253.8,
          "en": "Typically this variable is called I,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 253.8,
          "end": 258.39,
          "en": "but the name is up to you and it's set to an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.39,
          "end": 260.82,
          "en": "Very often that value will be zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.82,
          "end": 263.7,
          "en": "but any value can be used here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 263.7,
          "end": 267.27,
          "en": "Then thereafter you add a semicolon, so not a comma,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 267.27,
          "end": 268.65,
          "en": "but a semicolon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 268.65,
          "end": 271.83,
          "en": "which might look like a strange place since thus far",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.83,
          "end": 274.65,
          "en": "we always use semicolons at the end of lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.65,
          "end": 277.08,
          "en": "Now we're using it here in the middle of a line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.08,
          "end": 280.08,
          "en": "But that is just how the for loop must be defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.08,
          "end": 281.90999999999997,
          "en": "And we continue with the next piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 281.90999999999997,
          "end": 284.22,
          "en": "of configuration for the for loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 284.22,
          "end": 286.62,
          "en": "And that next piece of information that we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.62,
          "end": 289.252,
          "en": "to add here is a condition that controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 289.252,
          "end": 292.503,
          "en": "how long this loop should keep on running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 297.65999999999997,
          "en": "For that, you typically use this helper variable here, I.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.65999999999997,
          "end": 300.54,
          "en": "And here, I want to keep on running as long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.54,
          "end": 303.273,
          "en": "as I'm still processing chosen answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.23,
          "end": 307.11,
          "en": "So as long as I is smaller,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 307.11,
          "end": 309.36,
          "en": "and it's a new kind of comparison operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.36,
          "end": 310.89,
          "en": "which you haven't seen before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 310.89,
          "end": 314.04,
          "en": "but just as two equal signs can be used to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.04,
          "end": 317.67,
          "en": "for equality, smaller can be used to check whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 317.67,
          "end": 320.7,
          "en": "this value on the left side is smaller than",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 320.7,
          "end": 322.98,
          "en": "the value on the right side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 322.98,
          "end": 325.83,
          "en": "And the value on the right side here should be my",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 325.83,
          "end": 328.08,
          "en": "chosen answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 328.08,
          "end": 330.24,
          "en": "And there the length of this list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 330.24,
          "end": 333.6,
          "en": "which also will be a number, just like I.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 333.6,
          "end": 337.05,
          "en": "So now with this code, the loop here, which we are about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 337.05,
          "end": 340.17,
          "en": "to define, will keep on running as long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.17,
          "end": 345.09000000000003,
          "en": "as I is smaller than the length of my chosen answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 345.09000000000003,
          "end": 348.99,
          "en": "So if I have six answers in this list, this will be true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 348.99,
          "end": 351.72,
          "en": "as long as I is smaller than six,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 351.72,
          "end": 355.173,
          "en": "which it initially will be since we initialize it to zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 356.04,
          "end": 358.56,
          "en": "And therefore we need a third part here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 358.56,
          "end": 362.1,
          "en": "when configuring this list, where we actually control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 362.1,
          "end": 366.42,
          "en": "how I should change after every iteration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 366.42,
          "end": 369.72,
          "en": "Because if it never changes, we create an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 369.72,
          "end": 372.9,
          "en": "since I then would always be smaller than the length",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 372.9,
          "end": 373.833,
          "en": "of this list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 374.91,
          "end": 378.48,
          "en": "Therefore here, you then control how I should change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 378.48,
          "end": 381.42,
          "en": "And typically you increment I by one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 384.45,
          "en": "by using this ++ shortcut here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 384.45,
          "end": 388.38,
          "en": "You could also set it to I+1 like this manually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 388.38,
          "end": 389.943,
          "en": "but this is simply shorter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 391.2,
          "end": 394.11,
          "en": "And then you add opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 394.11,
          "end": 395.97,
          "en": "And between those curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 395.97,
          "end": 399.45,
          "en": "you have your loop body, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 399.45,
          "end": 402.03,
          "en": "And that will be the code that will be repeated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 402.03,
          "end": 405.813,
          "en": "until this condition here is not met anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 407.1,
          "end": 409.98,
          "en": "And in here, between these curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 409.98,
          "end": 413.613,
          "en": "I now want to add items to this list here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 414.75,
          "end": 417.33,
          "en": "So for that, I reach out to this summary list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 417.33,
          "end": 420.51,
          "en": "and call the add method to add items to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 420.51,
          "end": 423.39,
          "en": "And as you learn, you can do this on final lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 423.39,
          "end": 426.9,
          "en": "Just reassigning this to a new value wouldn't work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 426.9,
          "end": 428.733,
          "en": "but calling add will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 429.63,
          "end": 433.11,
          "en": "And the value I wanna add here is such a map.",
